sion was made and we'll  deal with the possibilities in a minute  but if the decision was made  to integrate a trans narrative into  vania's story in umbrella academy  it there may not be the time to work in  a completely from the ground  up edition or anything that would  require  new locations new actors not already  cast and things like that because even  though shooting doesn't start to  february between now and then  is when the logistics are worked out  schedules are locked down  locations are secured etc etc however  that would not preclude them from  altering scenes and  rewriting certain things to allow for  that narrative to be worked into  whatever else is already going on  so long as it doesn't require new  locations new characters etc  because that kind of stuff also ups your  budget  so there is time for them to do any  number of things  but the questions that come up are  can elliot  a trans non-binary person  play what has up to this point been a  cisgender  woman and the answer to that is of  course he freaking can  now i'm not even going to entertain  the whole oh what you're saying a trans  person can play a cis  part but you've said before that cis  actors can't play trans people yes i  have and  refresh yourself on the video  where i talked about that because i'm  not i'm not entertaining that argument  here  yes he can play a cis woman  no cis people can't play trans  characters  not right now no so let's tackle  some of the things that i see being  brought up mostly  this first one especially is almost  always in bad faith the idea often gets  floated that  he couldn't play vinya because it would  give him dysphoria to play a woman  first of all i hate seeing that come up  it's one of the things i've been meaning  to tackle for a while  dysphoria is incredibly  personal and specific to every  individual who experiences it  a b not every trans person has dysphoria  or at least not severe dysphoria it's  part of the  narrative in pop culture that people  transition because  their dysphoria is so bad that's what  they have to do that is  not the truth for all trans people  and let us not forget  elliot is an actor it is not  unreasonable to assume  he's capable of taking on a part without  it triggering dysphoria  is it possible for  elliot or any trans actor to experience  debilitating dysphoria by having to  portray  a gender that they once were forced to  present  as and may have trauma related to that  yes  that is possible but you cannot take it  as a given  unless elliot says i can't play a cis  woman because of my dysphoria then this  option isn't on the table  you don't get to decide in advance that  he can't play this part because of that  only he can say whether or not dysphoria  is an issue for him  so drop that one so unless he says  otherwise elliot is  absolutely fully capable of slipping  back in to the character of vinya and  playing vinya  as a cis woman  it's also an option to introduce trans  elements into the character  anyone who brings up the idea that well  they can't do that because that's not  being true to the character  uh hold up do you have any idea how many  changes have already been made to these  characters in this adaptation  sticking on vinya specifically buying  his sexuality so far as i could find is  never  addressed in the comics and yet she is  now established as  being bisexual in the show  so we've already deviated right there  in the comic all of these characters are  white  like really white we have a very  mixed ethnicity group in the show  they're not obligated to stay true to  every single detail  of these characters they're allowed to  do their own thing they already have  done with vanya with her entire  story and character arc in the second  season  was based around material not in the  comics  so if your concern is it's not being  true to the character you shouldn't even  be watching the show anymore you would  have had to have written it off  heck season one definitely season two  so don't come at me with that one  umbrella academy has a  unique opportunity to integrate  a trans actor's story and life  experience  into a character not originally designed  for that story  but you can still bring those things in  i've talked about this thing  sort of thing before when i talked about  characters who were  turned gay later in their life but were  not originally written to be that at  their initial conception there's the  thing so there is a validity to doing  that because a lot of people  either come to a realization about  themselves later in life  or even if they don't they don't come  out until later in life as  elliot himself is evidence of  that having been said just because they  have the opportunity doesn't mean that  they have to take it  maybe elliott doesn't want his  transition to be highlighted in the work  that he does  maybe they can't figure out a way to  integrate it cleanly  there's any number of reasons for them  to not do it  so i also want to be clear that while i  think it's an opportunity and i  would kind of like to see it addressed  in some  fashion the show isn't obligated to and  i would not be  mad at it if it doesn't  because it's still the same character  it's still the same actor who is very  good in the part  how that actor is identifying away from  the part  having changed doesn't affect  any of that so those were all the major  points that i wanted to hit in talking  about  elliott having come out and it's ripple  effects on  umbrella academy so  thank you for listening be polite use  correct pronouns  don't dead name  and we'll all move forward so thank you  very much  for watching usual stuff like share  subscribe  got a patreon it's how i pay my bills  and it is greatly appreciated keeps the  lights on around here  but you also don't have to do any of it  because end of the day  you are the council i just run the  meetings  and until next time this council is  [Music]  adjourned  [Music